in the dark mines, step by step, delaying each step for a second to
be sure that you don't bump into a floating eye, your patience (and
copious time to play) are stressed a lot. I try to do that as much
as possible, but that's extreme. You call failing all that stupid?

For me a stupid move - that leads to a stupid death - is something
where your "stupid" brain comes to a wrong conclusion despite you
should know better. I certainly know that it's stupid to run into
a floating eye. I certainly don't do that deliberately because I'd
think it would be a good idea to tarket one hit for an instant kill
chance at it. No. But accidents happen.

In the past I've posted quite a few really stupid moves (and YASDs)
here. If you need a repost of some examples just ask.[**]

