cubes would be a lot more dangerous than eyes. And this is plain
wrong. Along the line of the argument "don't bump into eyes" you
can also say "don't come close to cubes". Does that lead anywhere?
No; both are quite stupid arguments that don't help judging about
the actual danger of cubes and eyes in a practical game.

YMMV, of course.

